      "sha": "c71dc825105c7400fdb19b49c400fd14e81fd8ea",
        "message": "Add test: SAMPLE / SAMPLE OFFSET survive the serialized-plan round-trip\n\nAddress review: the changelog claims a fix for both FINAL and SAMPLE under\n`serialize_query_plan = 1`, but the regression in\n04509_hash_table_sizes_stats_table_functions only exercised FINAL. Add\n04612_serialize_query_plan_table_function_sample: a MergeTree table with\n`SAMPLE BY intHash32(k)` read via `cluster('test_shard_localhost', merge(...))`\nwith `serialize_query_plan = 1, prefer_localhost_replica = 0`, covering the\nfull read, `SAMPLE 1/2`, and `SAMPLE 1/2 OFFSET 1/2`. The sampling is\ndeterministic, so the reference pins the exact counts (10000 / 4972 / 5028;\nthe two complementary samples partition the table). If `resolveStorages`\ndropped `sample_size` / `sample_offset` on the worker, both sampled reads\nwould return 10000.",
          "sha": "2269d745800cbd7237794bd3997b3e5ba4602a97"
          "sha": "f2bc3168cca87acec3bed582614b007e4abb3a6f"
      "sha": "20dea4f5e66f9829e32a856802e9f3a2100b7632",
        "message": "Isolate 00180_no_seek_avoiding_when_reading_from_cache from other cache users\n\nThe test asserts that its measured query reads entirely from the filesystem\ncache, but the table is created with `CREATE TABLE hits_s3_sampled AS\ntest.hits_s3`, so it inherits `storage_policy = 's3_cache'`: the single 200 MiB\ncache shared by everything on the server. Background merges of `test.hits_s3`\nwrite through that cache and can fill it with file segments held open by a\n`FileSegmentsHolder`, which are not releasable. The warm-up queries' space\nreservation then finds nothing to evict, silently continues without caching, and\nthe measured query reads from S3, so `CachedReadBufferReadFromSourceBytes` is\nnon-zero. `SYSTEM CLEAR FILESYSTEM CACHE` does not help, since it is\n`removeAllReleasable` and skips held segments.\n\nGive the table a private inline cache disk instead, keyed on\n`$CLICKHOUSE_DATABASE` so the disk name is unique per run and the test stays\nparallel-safe, and scope the cache clear to that cache. The assertion, the\nreference file and the tags are unchanged.\n\n`04695_filesystem_cache_wait_for_concurrent_download_timeout.sh` was isolated\nthe same way in eca7e2270696c02 for this same mechanism.\n\nThe explicit `ENGINE = MergeTree` is required. Without it, `setEngine` calls\n`inheritStorageFromSource`, whose `mergeStorageSettings` appends the source's\n`storage_policy` next to the new `disk` setting, and `loadFromQuery` then throws\n`storage_policy and disk cannot be specified at the same time`. With the engine\ngiven explicitly that path is skipped, while columns and the PARTITION BY /\nORDER BY / SAMPLE BY clauses are still copied from the source table.\n\nValidated by reproducing the failure mode locally with a concurrent workload\nthat keeps the shared cache full of held segments, confirmed by a global cache\nclear leaving 229.68 MiB across 46 segments resident. Runs of the real test file\nunder that workload: 2 of 20 passed before this change, 50 of 50 after. With the\nsame query and settings against a cold cache the asserted counters are 4607579\nand 7944923, and against the warm private cache both are 0, so the assertion\nstill catches the regression it exists for.\n\nCloses: https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/issues/114213",
          "sha": "818aec27dce589469b39b55f5b266196cdb7f1f1"
          "sha": "106a589824ffda289c008302d270f1e7da1c731b"
      "sha": "af647baeb2ac1f1c4448b5916430441427aaa208",
